{"y":1993,"label":"1992–93","coach":"Jim Calhoun","conf":"Big East","confShort":"Big East","w":15,"l":13,"cw":9,"cl":9,"confFinish":"4th in Big East","finish":"nit","apPre":16,"apHigh":15,"srs":11.69,"sos":8.05,"ortg":98.7,"drtg":94.0,"ppg":75.5,"oppg":71.8,"story":{"headline":"A Pause Before the Surge","text":"The 1992–93 Huskies slipped to 15–13 and 9–9 in the Big East, the lone non-NCAA season between 1990 and 1996. There were moments — an 81–80 win at No. 17 Pittsburgh in February chief among them — and Donyell Marshall blossomed into a first-team All-Big East forward. But Providence ended UConn's Big East tournament in the quarterfinals, 73–55, and the NIT trip lasted one night: a 90–88 overtime loss to Jackson State. Senior Scott Burrell, the first player in NCAA history to compile 1,500 points, 750 rebounds, 275 assists and 300 steals, went 20th overall to the Charlotte Hornets in the 1993 NBA draft — a two-sport star who had also been drafted by baseball's Toronto Blue Jays and spent two summers in the minor leagues.","moments":[{"date":"1993-03-19","title":"NIT First Round: L vs Jackson State","text":"UConn lost to Jackson State 88–90 (OT) (First Round) at Harry A. Gampel Pavilion, Storrs, Connecticut."}],"honors":["Donyell Marshall – First-team All-Big East"],"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1992%E2%80%9393_Connecticut_Huskies_men's_basketball_team","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UConn_Huskies_men%27s_basketball","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scott_Burrell"]},"roster":[{"pid":"donyell-marshall-1","name":"Donyell Marshall","num":"42","cls":"SO","pos":"F","ht":"6-9","wt":218,"home":"Reading, PA","photo":"assets/players/donyell-marshall-1.jpg?v=446c056c","photoWide":true,"pg":{"g":27,"gs":26,"mp":31.6,"pts":17.0,"trb":7.8,"ast":1.1,"stl":1.4,"blk":2.1,"tov":2.2,"fg_pct":0.5,"fg3_pct":0.37,"ft_pct":0.829,"orb":null,"pf":2.3},"tot":{"mp":854,"fg":166,"fga":332,"fg3":20,"fg3a":54,"ft":107,"fta":129,"orb":null,"drb":null,"trb":210,"ast":30,"stl":39,"blk